#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:5
#: 95bd7fb9e9484d4d81bdc845cd547199
msgid "Airspeed Parameters Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:10
#: 12fe79f0f8f147fbba4044891cd9b437
msgid "Speed Scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:12
#: 84ec44b81c0443a5b2c170d280857e5f
msgid "Since the effect of flying surface control deflection increases and decreases with airspeed, the stabilization gains in the PID loops are automatically scaled with airspeed by ArduPilot to prevent oscillations at higher airspeeds and preserve stabilization effectiveness at low airspeeds, even if no airspeed sensor is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:14
#: f4c27078a60b44a5a145d129198e7b56
msgid "This is accomplished by ArduPilot estimating airspeed from other sensor inputs like GPS velocity, position changes, and IMU accelerations. This estimate is also used in case an airspeed sensor is used and becomes unhealthy. In systems without an airspeed sensor this estimate is used for speed scaling of the PID loops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:16
#: 210e14361250404ba0586ace155272eb
msgid "So, even if an airspeed sensor is not present, some airspeed parameters are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:18
#: 455a1a585fab44c8a1b37a12e0261a94
msgid "Normally, the default values are acceptable, but very fast or very slow vehicles may need them adjusted for best performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:21
#: 971504321ac34a7d9a11984956941d65
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:23
#: b194ecfe7e2840ec8cb81063733679d6
msgid "Key parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:25
#: fffbe47041414781b6f5453b118fbb32
msgid ":ref:`AIRSPEED_MAX<AIRSPEED_MAX>`: This is the fastest normal flying speed for the vehicle. Normally, 2 times the nominal cruising speed is a good target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:26
#: 04f24dce36494be7b5eed1d21030b70a
msgid ":ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN<AIRSPEED_MIN>`: This is the slowest flying speed for the vehicle. It should be set at least 25% above the stall speed of the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:27
#: 9dcd1b9b65534df495db8a0de27797dd
msgid ":ref:`SCALING_SPEED<SCALING_SPEED>`: This is the center of the speed scaling range and should be set close to the normal cruising speed of the vehicle. PID tuning (see :ref:`tuning-quickstart`) should be done at this flying speed. The loop gains are scaled above and below this value with a multiplier determined base on the above min and max flying speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:29
#: 4e1ace09011b4e8e979004eb0501ccf3
msgid "The above parameters determine the speed scaling characteristics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:31
#: 482bf667fa164d6391fa280d2a40b523
msgid "You must set the :ref:`SCALING_SPEED<SCALING_SPEED>` before doing any tuning, since changing this after tuning directly scales the effect of the tuned PID values and will corrupt the tune, possibly leading to instability. If you need to change this after tuning to match your vehicle's nominal cruise speed for some reason, revert the PID values back to their default values before flying and retune again at the normal cruising speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:34
#: 4c7c6c6dbc8b4135b44092acd08a2232
msgid "And, if you use an airspeed sensor:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:36
#: 2e2434c8451e4a6e93eb5ee30e13b952
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>`: This determines the type of sensor used. Set to \"0\" if no sensor is present. (see :ref:`airspeed`). If non-zero and the sensor is healthy, the system will use the sensor's measurements instead of the estimated speed calculation for speed scaling and speed controlled modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:37
#: 8d4c374923af438db33181a931c3d679
msgid ":ref:`AIRSPEED_CRUISE<AIRSPEED_CRUISE>`: This determines the nominal cruising speed in AUTO/GUIDED speed controlled modes when using an airspeed sensor. (see :ref:`tuning-cruise` ). Also see :ref:`tuning-cruise` section if not using an airspeed sensor for the impact of the parameter - :ref:`TRIM_THROTTLE<TRIM_THROTTLE>` on cruising speed in speed controlled modes like CRUISE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:40
#: d5a214be96a14f4d9e80db231e3907c0
msgid "ARSPD_USE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:42
#: 818a1de80cf84883bf8425867ae10911
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` determines if the airspeed estimate is used in other ArduPlane functions besides speed scaling. If no airspeed sensor is present and :ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` =1, then the estimated airspeed will be used as if was obtained via an accurate airspeed sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airspeed-parameters-setup.rst:44
#: 71a51f0929ba41288e84e221c1e982fb
msgid "using the estimated airspeed for speed controlled modes by enabling :ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` without an airspeed sensor can result in erratic, or even dangerous, operation since the estimate can be wrong in situations like automatic takeoffs into a strong headwind, or when flying into the wind for an extended period without making any turns (which updates the wind speed estimate and therefore the estimated airspeed)."
msgstr ""
